Incomplete list...

boots - PROS: don't occupy ring slot, CONS: you won't have very high
speed while wearing them, can be stripped of by monsters, or, (if no
MR) disintegrated, you typically have less AC while wearing them (if
you've no spare enchant armor for them).

rings - PROS: you still have extra speed from boots, CONS: can be
destroyed by shock attacks (e.g. electric eels), or stolen/stripped off
by some monsters

potion - PROS: intrinsic property, you don't lose it on monster action,
doesn't require ring slot or boots slot, CONS: will last only a certain
amount of turns and randomly wears off (used a blessed potion for a good
guaranteed minimum of 200(?) turns and the possibility to terminate
levitation at will ('>'))

spell - I've no experience here, but I suppose it's intrinsic similar to
potions

